!-   ===========  ALL OBJECTS IN CLASS: SCHEDULETYPELIMITS ===========

! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits (all 5 objects of this class): not in the documents. Kept: prototype values.
! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits "On/Off": not in the xlsx or the PDF. Kept: an EnergyPlus input rule (0 to 1, discrete) that only lets EnergyPlus check the range and the numeric type of the schedule values; it is not a building input and changes no result. For schedules whose values are 0 (off) or 1 (on).
  ScheduleTypeLimits,
    On/Off,                  !- Name
    0,                       !- Lower Limit Value
    1,                       !- Upper Limit Value
    Discrete;                !- Numeric Type

! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits "Fraction": not in the xlsx or the PDF. Kept: an EnergyPlus input rule (0 to 1, continuous) that only lets EnergyPlus check the range and the numeric type of the schedule values; it is not a building input and changes no result. For schedules whose values are fractions of a design level (between 0 and 1).
  ScheduleTypeLimits,
    Fraction,                !- Name
    0,                       !- Lower Limit Value
    1,                       !- Upper Limit Value
    Continuous;              !- Numeric Type

! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits "Temperature": not in the xlsx or the PDF. Kept: an EnergyPlus input rule (-100 to 100, continuous) that only lets EnergyPlus check the range and the numeric type of the schedule values; it is not a building input and changes no result. Generic range for temperature schedules (the set points); the EnergyPlus example files use -60 to 200 C; why these numbers is not documented, it is a wide range that no real temperature leaves.
  ScheduleTypeLimits,
    Temperature,             !- Name
    -100,                    !- Lower Limit Value
    100,                     !- Upper Limit Value
    Continuous;              !- Numeric Type

! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits "Any Number": not in the xlsx or the PDF. Kept: an EnergyPlus input rule (no limits) that only lets EnergyPlus check the range and the numeric type of the schedule values; it is not a building input and changes no result. No limits: any number is accepted.
  ScheduleTypeLimits,
    Any Number;              !- Name

! Source for ScheduleTypeLimits "Control Type": not in the xlsx or the PDF. Kept: an EnergyPlus input rule (0 to 4, discrete) that only lets EnergyPlus check the range and the numeric type of the schedule values; it is not a building input and changes no result. Limits of the thermostat control type schedule of ZoneControl:Thermostat: the schedule value is a code, 0 = uncontrolled, 1 = single heating set point, 2 = single cooling set point, 3 = single heating / cooling set point, 4 = dual set point with dead band (heating and cooling); so the range is 0 to 4 and the type is discrete (whole numbers). The code meanings are those of the EnergyPlus input rules as understood here, not checked against the Input Output Reference.
  ScheduleTypeLimits,
    Control Type,            !- Name
    0,                       !- Lower Limit Value
    4,                       !- Upper Limit Value
    Discrete;                !- Numeric Type

